One annoying aspect of this is that once this implicit type is created, newly created tables and types with the same name can move it out of the way! For example,

```
create type t as enum ();
// Implicit array type _t is created.
create table _t (x t);
// Succeeds!
// _t is renamed to __t.
```
Wow! and if you rename `_t`, then `__t` will shift back into the open slot `_t`...
```
alter table _t rename to tbl;
// __t gets implicitly renamed back to _t
```
